   "body": "**mac/M1: still flaky with serial tests (after #847), 2026-11-12.** `aRemovalInFlightIsNotSentTwice()` fails at `TopicRowActionsTests.swift:226:9` (`writer.removed.count == 1`), on three PRs that touch nothing in its area:\n- CI, App build + tests job: #809 run 43310087211 (6688c585) and #804 run 43311366056 (c10d936d).\n- Local `xcodebuild build test`, iOS 27.0, `-parallel-testing-enabled NO`: once each on #850 (iPhone 18 Pro), #809 (iPad Pro 11-inch M5) and #804 (iPhone 18 Pro), about 1 run in 3 overall.\n- Suite-only reruns (`-only-testing:SwiftHFRTests/TopicRowActionsTests`): 3/3 green on #850's iPhone; 2/3 green on #809's iPad, the third failing the same way.\n\nSo serial testing did not remove it, and it now costs reruns of the macOS App job. A timing dependency inside the test itself (the second removal reaching the writer before the in-flight guard is set) looks more likely than load from other tests. This is a reading of the failure, not checked in the code.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
